<Base title="About" description="Adam Fishman is an independent software engineer in Cleveland with 17+ years of building platforms, integrations and products.">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I'm Adam Fishman. Otoro Systems is my independent software practice, based in Lakewood, Ohio, just outside Cleveland.</p>
    <p>I've been building software for more than 17 years, across healthcare, fintech, e-commerce, retail and beverage tech. Some of that work started from a blank page. A lot of it started with a system the business already depended on, and the job was to make it better: move it to a modern stack, connect it to partners, or get its data into people's hands.</p>
    <p>I like owning the whole arc. On a new product that means talking through the idea, choosing the architecture, building the backend and the front end, and staying through launch. On an older one it means learning how the code really works, then moving it forward without breaking what runs on it.</p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>I work directly with your team, as a hands-on engineer and, when it helps, as a technical lead. I use modern AI-driven development every day, with Claude Code and agentic workflows, to research, prototype and ship faster. It speeds up the work. It doesn't replace judgment, testing or review.</p>

    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Languages: Java, TypeScript and JavaScript, Python, Ruby, SQL</li>
      <li>Frameworks: Ruby on Rails, Spring Boot, React, Vue, Django, Node, Astro</li>
      <li>Cloud: AWS, Azure, Cloudflare (Workers, D1, R2)</li>
      <li>Data: PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, ETL pipelines and REST APIs</li>
      <li>Learning now: Elixir and Phoenix</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Outside the code</h2>
    <p>Cleveland is home, and I plan to keep it that way. From 2012 to 2016 I owned Tremont Scoops, an ice cream parlor. I'm drawn to work where technology meets craft, and to projects that make a difference close to home.</p>
    <p>I studied computer engineering at Virginia Tech.</p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Get in touch →</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
